\newlabel{tab:main}{{IV}{6}{Deterministic reference rows, 80 scenarios (20 per family), rule set R2. Naive roles do not know the rules; procedural roles follow them. Att.\ viol.\ and Exec.\ viol.\ are attempted and executed violations per episode; Overseer is the number of approval requests reaching the human per episode; Silent viol.\ is the share of successful episodes with an executed violation; Hidden harm the share of episodes with an approval-required action executed where the human would have refused}{table.4}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Overseer load against hidden harm for static and trust-adaptive governance, rule set R3, hidden context in 15\% of scenarios. Points on each line are thresholds 0.9, 0.7, 0.5, 0.3 and 0.0 from right to left; for the procedural roles the four lowest coincide.}}{6}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:tradeoff}{{2}{6}{Overseer load against hidden harm for static and trust-adaptive governance, rule set R3, hidden context in 15\% of scenarios. Points on each line are thresholds 0.9, 0.7, 0.5, 0.3 and 0.0 from right to left; for the procedural roles the four lowest coincide}{figure.2}{}}
